# Core workflow

Before writing application code on a **new** project (or a major greenfield area):

1. Create or align standard project structure
2. Create or update required documentation (`docs/`)
3. Create or update project-specific Cursor rules (`.cursor/rules/`)
4. Define scripts layout (`scripts/`) — document commands; avoid one-off duplicates
5. Maintain architecture entrypoint (`docs/architecture/README.md`)
6. Define stack and architectural direction
7. Match existing repo conventions

Prioritize: maintainability, readability, scalability, modularity, consistency, documentation.

## AI agent behavior

- Read relevant `docs/` and `.cursor/rules/` before non-trivial changes
- Extend existing services; do not introduce parallel systems without reason
- Update docs when architecture or operations change
- Do not change architecture silently or add frameworks without justification
- Never commit secrets; use env vars and documented secret mounts

## Philosophy

Simplicity over complexity; extensibility over hacks; consistency over novelty; operational visibility and developer experience.
